      "summaries": {
        "en": "Music Assistant is an open-source media library manager that unifies your streaming services and smart speakers into a single, coherent system. Its server component runs on always-on devices like Raspberry Pi or NAS, acting as the central hub for music playback and library management. Technically, it uses a plugin architecture to support diverse streaming sources and speaker protocols, enabling seamless cross-platform control. You can deploy it on a home server to manage Spotify, Tidal, local files, and multi-room audio from one interface, making it ideal for building a private, integrated music ecosystem.",
        "zh": "Music Assistant 是一个开源媒体库管理器，通过插件架构整合流媒体服务（如 Spotify、Tidal）与智能音箱协议，实现跨平台无缝控制。其服务器组件需运行于树莓派、NAS 等常开设备，作为音乐播放与库管理的核心枢纽。用户可部署于家用服务器，通过单一界面管理本地音乐、在线曲库及多房间音频，构建私有集成音乐生态。该方案适合希望摆脱封闭生态、自主掌控音乐体验的用户。",
        "es": "Music Assistant is an open-source media library manager that unifies your streaming services and smart speakers into a single, coherent system. Its server component runs on always-on devices like Raspberry Pi or NAS, acting as the central hub for music playback and library management. Technically, it uses a plugin architecture to support diverse streaming sources and speaker protocols, enabling seamless cross-platform control. You can deploy it on a home server to manage Spotify, Tidal, local files, and multi-room audio from one interface, making it ideal for building a private, integrated music ecosystem.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "server gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Music Assistant is an open-source media library manager that unifies your streaming services and smart speakers into a single, coherent system. Its server component runs on always-on devices like Raspberry Pi or NAS, acting as the central hub for music playback and library management. Technically, it uses a plugin architecture to support diverse streaming sources and speaker protocols, enabling seamless cross-platform control. You can deploy it on a home server to manage Spotify, Tidal, local files, and multi-room audio from one interface, making it ideal for building a private, integrated music ecosystem.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/music-assistant/server for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
